From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the taskbar's magnifier, Start mark and Glass orb are drawn smooth

GDI draws lines, ellipses, polygons and clip paths without antialiasing,
and the taskbar drew its own art with them: the search button's
magnifier, the Start mark's four panes and the Glass look's round orb had
stepped, jagged edges, which a scaled bar (150%, or a 1080p screen) made
worse (David 2026-10-05: the search icon and the Glass orb looked "low
quality").

sg_smooth draws a piece of art four times larger on black, averages it
down to pixels -- each as opaque as the share of it drawn on -- and blends
it in, so edges are soft, as Windows' own drawn glyphs are. The magnifier
(now sized with the bar, SG_PX), the Start mark (on every look) and the
whole Glass orb go through it; the orb's mark is drawn smooth on top.

Test: test/smoothicons-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_JAGGED_MARK,
SG_MUTANT_JAGGED_MAGNIFIER, SG_MUTANT_JAGGED_ORB each fail it)
---
